              "anchor_line": 460,
              "category": "correctness",
              "consequence": "A recurring cancellation can return success before the external calendar events are deleted. In serverless runtimes the work may be cut off, leaving stale events in the calendar. A failing deleteEvent becomes an unhandled promise rejection that can crash the Node process.",
              "explanation": "For a recurring cancel with allRemainingBookings, the calendar deletions are done inside `.forEach(async (credential) => {...})`. forEach does not wait for async callbacks. The change adds `await getCalendar(credential)` inside it, so each callback now suspends before any `deleteEvent` call and before `apiDeletes.push(deletedEvent)`. The surrounding handler continues, and whatever later does `Promise.all(apiDeletes)` sees an empty or partial array. The deleteEvent calls therefore are not awaited, and their rejections are unhandled instead of being caught with the other integration errors.",
              "id": "finding-3e8c1dd96eb9f10adf0eeed5",
              "lines": [
                243,
                589
              ],
              "path": "packages/features/bookings/lib/handleCancelBooking.ts",
              "severity": "p1",
              "title": "Recurring-booking calendar deletions run in a non-awaited async forEach"
            },
            {
              "anchor_line": 553,
              "category": "correctness",
              "consequence": "The mutation can complete before the old calendar events and meetings are removed, so the previous slot can stay blocked. A failure in deleteEvent or deleteMeeting is an unhandled rejection that can crash the process, or the work can be cut short in serverless runtimes.",
              "explanation": "`bookingRefsFiltered.forEach(async (bookingRef) => {...})` now awaits getCalendar and then returns `calendar.deleteEvent(...)` or `deleteMeeting(...)`. forEach discards the returned promises, so nothing waits for the deletions or handles their errors. The mutation goes on to send the reschedule emails and webhooks and then returns.",
