            {
              "anchor_line": 161,
              "category": "correctness",
              "consequence": "With passkeys enabled, the regular username/password login page no longer offers conditional passkey (autofill) login. Passkey login is effectively broken for the main flow.",
              "explanation": "The old checks were `context.getUser() == null && webauthnAuth != null && webauthnAuth.isPasskeysEnabled()`, and the old `authenticate` code only ran inside the branch where the user was not yet set. The new helper `isConditionalPasskeysEnabled(UserModel user)` returns `webauthnAuth != null && webauthnAuth.isPasskeysEnabled() && user != null`. On a normal login `context.getUser()` is null, so the helper returns false. `authenticate` and `challenge(context, error, field)` then skip `webauthnAuth.fillContextForm(context)`. The conditional-UI passkey attributes (challenge, rpId, ENABLE_WEBAUTHN_CONDITIONAL_UI) are therefore never put on the username/password form. They are only set when a user is already known, which is the re-authentication case. In that case the first lookup in `challenge()` happens only after getUser/clearUser has run during validation.",
